meta {
  name: logout (GET)
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/rest-auth/logout/
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessTokenStudent}}
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  **Use `POST /rest-auth/logout/` instead** -- see **logout**.

  This version of dj-rest-auth (5.0.1) no longer accepts GET here -- it returns
  **405 Method Not Allowed**. Older releases did, which is why the route still
  answers at all.

  It is listed only so the collection covers every method the server exposes. A
  GET that logs someone out was always a bad idea anyway: browser prefetchers and
  link scanners follow GETs.

  ## API example response
  {
    "detail": "Method \"GET\" not allowed."
  }
}
